{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And a lament.</b> Kinot [elegies]." "<b>Yotza.</b> From the heavy [binyan] with dagesh, the augmented [binyan], and the missing letter is yod, like the yod in אצוק מים. But the right view in my eyes is that the yod is a root letter, like the yod in יולד, and it is from the heavy [binyan] with dagesh whose [active] participle is not called [by the expected form]. There are in the words of an individual that Hatakh is Daniel, but it seems unlikely to me that his days extended until the reign of Ahasuerus, for he was old, and the distinction of wisdom would not depart."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:58.141489522Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}